WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.436
(harp glissando)

00:00:02.436 --> 00:00:04.944
- We've done hands that have webs

00:00:04.944 --> 00:00:06.207
in between them.

00:00:06.207 --> 00:00:07.173
Horns,

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.662
spikes,

00:00:08.662 --> 00:00:10.357
lizard feet, Viking boots,

00:00:10.357 --> 00:00:11.323
whiskers,

00:00:11.323 --> 00:00:12.461
teeth.

00:00:12.461 --> 00:00:13.840
There is no mascot handbook,

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.604
and, if there is, there shouldn't be.

00:00:16.604 --> 00:00:19.854
My name is Brittany, and I make mascots.

00:00:22.399 --> 00:00:25.044
Olympus Group was founded in 1893.

00:00:25.044 --> 00:00:30.044
It's located in beautiful
North Milwaukee, Wisconsin.

00:00:30.253 --> 00:00:31.487
Each mascot is different.

00:00:31.487 --> 00:00:33.213
It's such a art form.

00:00:33.213 --> 00:00:34.319
It definitely takes a lot of passion;

00:00:34.319 --> 00:00:35.604
it takes a lot of creativity;

00:00:35.604 --> 00:00:36.573
it takes a lot of teamwork;

00:00:36.573 --> 00:00:38.658
and the people who work here are

00:00:38.658 --> 00:00:41.301
absolutely amazing with what they can do.

00:00:41.301 --> 00:00:43.773
There's Molly, she's the
Head Fabrication Technician.

00:00:43.773 --> 00:00:46.229
Steve, he's the Sketch
and Sculpting Artist.

00:00:46.229 --> 00:00:49.143
Sally is the Engineering
and the Prepress Specialist.

00:00:49.143 --> 00:00:51.405
Mary is the Foam Fabrication Technician,

00:00:51.405 --> 00:00:54.107
and Lyssa is the
Patterning and Sewing Lead.

00:00:54.107 --> 00:00:55.207
And then there's Mitchell.

00:00:55.207 --> 00:00:57.624
He usually delivers us lunch.

00:01:00.451 --> 00:01:01.770
(bell dings)

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.028
Whenever we get a request in,

00:01:03.028 --> 00:01:05.724
we get around a table and
we come up with a plan.

00:01:05.724 --> 00:01:08.800
The request can be anything
from a detailed presentation

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:12.013
to a doodle on a cocktail napkin.

00:01:12.013 --> 00:01:14.797
The sketch team will sketch up
a rendering for the customer

00:01:14.797 --> 00:01:17.170
and then we'll send
that out for approvals.

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:19.580
After that's settled, we eat.

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.079
Lunch is very important.

00:01:21.079 --> 00:01:23.158
We have tight deadlines.

00:01:23.158 --> 00:01:25.588
We can't always get out
and sit down at lunch.

00:01:25.588 --> 00:01:27.005
So sometimes it's really helpful to

00:01:27.005 --> 00:01:29.692
be able to get delivery to
help us through our day.

00:01:29.692 --> 00:01:31.790
Collaboration is super important.

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:34.069
There's no one person that
can make a whole costume.

00:01:34.069 --> 00:01:35.650
First, it will go to the sculptor,

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:37.268
who sculpts the head.

00:01:37.268 --> 00:01:38.984
We'll turn that into a mold.

00:01:38.984 --> 00:01:40.777
The mold will then be vacuformed.

00:01:40.777 --> 00:01:43.439
It's kind of like something
out of a Sci-fi movie.

00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:44.926
It's a lot of fun to watch.

00:01:44.926 --> 00:01:47.504
Once the heads are vacuformed
and all put together,

00:01:47.504 --> 00:01:49.214
then, they go over to our technicians

00:01:49.214 --> 00:01:50.647
on our head covering team.

00:01:50.647 --> 00:01:51.759
They'll pull fabrics from the wall

00:01:51.759 --> 00:01:54.433
and begin gluing the fabric onto the head.

00:01:54.433 --> 00:01:56.401
And then it's a matter of cutting fabric,

00:01:56.401 --> 00:01:57.840
sewing it together,

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.241
adding, kind of, those
last finishing details

00:02:00.241 --> 00:02:01.699
to get the whole costume to come together

00:02:01.699 --> 00:02:03.366
to fit as one piece.

00:02:05.289 --> 00:02:06.927
Then we'll make sure it's able to

00:02:06.927 --> 00:02:09.039
meet all the necessary requirements

00:02:09.039 --> 00:02:10.401
the performer will need.

00:02:10.401 --> 00:02:11.591
- Jump!

00:02:11.591 --> 00:02:13.339
- [Brittany] As soon
as you put that head on.

00:02:13.339 --> 00:02:14.687
- Cry!

00:02:14.687 --> 00:02:17.445
- [Brittany] The person kind
of, like, becomes that character.

00:02:17.445 --> 00:02:18.701
- Dance!

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:20.069
- [Brittany] Some people
will start to dance

00:02:20.069 --> 00:02:21.310
and do poses.

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:24.039
They can be kind of larger than life.

00:02:24.039 --> 00:02:25.538
And then we'll do a photoshoot.

00:02:25.538 --> 00:02:27.056
(shutter clicking)

00:02:27.056 --> 00:02:29.508
It is just very cool to
kinda see the whole process

00:02:29.508 --> 00:02:31.092
all coming together and being finished.

00:02:31.092 --> 00:02:32.932
There's a ton of pride when
it comes to that moment.

00:02:32.932 --> 00:02:34.647
Once the mascot is complete,

00:02:34.647 --> 00:02:36.379
we'll go to wherever
the next cocktail napkin

00:02:36.379 --> 00:02:37.610
takes us.

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:39.860
(laughing)

